# English Developer Text & Strict ARB Localization

## 1. Comments, Docs, Logs & Commits (English Only)

- Write **all** source code comments (`//`, `/* */`, `///` Dartdoc), SQL comments, developer documentation (`docs/*.md`), diagnostic log messages, and `TODO`/`FIXME` notes strictly in **English**.
- Explain the non-obvious *why*, invariants, and platform caveats concisely. Do not narrate trivial syntax.
- Never write non-English text in comments or developer logs.
- Commit messages must follow **`git-commits.mdc`** in English.

---

## 2. User-Facing Copy (Arabic & English ARB Files Only)

- **Never** hardcode user-facing strings in widgets, BLoCs, services, or platform channels — neither English nor Arabic.
- Every user-facing label, button, title, hint, accessibility label (`Semantics`), tooltip, error message, toast, and dialog copy MUST live in:
  - `lib/l10n/app_en.arb` (English LTR)
  - `lib/l10n/app_ar.arb` (Arabic RTL — natural, Egyptian-friendly wording)
- Keep all keys 100% synchronized across `app_en.arb` and `app_ar.arb`, with explicit placeholders and ICU plural forms (`{count, plural, ...}`) where needed.
- Access localized strings via **`AppLocalizations.of(context)!.<key>`** (or `context.l10n.<key>` extension).
- Add new ARB keys and run `flutter gen-l10n` **before** building the UI widgets that consume them.
- **Exception (Dynamic User Content):** Track titles, artist/album names, embedded lyrics, folder names, and file paths read from device storage are displayed verbatim without translation, wrapped in proper bidi handling (see **`wetar-mandatory-design.mdc`**).
